## Context
DESIGN.md §4 item 14. One design conversation upstream, not four: the ledger
with signals-vs-keys (§2.1), the entries schema + slab references + segmenter
(§2.2, X5-gated), the lib-keyed store under the NEW FILENAME
search-index-v2.sqlite (concurrency F1: no protocol binds binaries that
predate it), the conductor protocol with both F-repairs in the text (worker
exits on stdin EOF + lease-holder check; lease renewal on a timer, renewed
before any long fetch), record-first frontier with the derived band cap K,
dual-embed migration with the lazy-load repair, and the counters + convergence
harness offered as the acceptance spec he can run against whatever he builds.
Opened AFTER the PR train (0014-0023), so the conversation starts from
merged, reviewed pieces rather than from a specification. Per C2 the
contract survives even if he reimplements the machinery in his own idiom —
that is where the durable value lives. Include the two ratification questions
for the author: R26's prefix granularity reading, and the 300 MB budget's
scoping under N processes (both flagged in DESIGN.md).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] X5 verdict in hand before the RFC quotes segmenter numbers
- [ ] RFC issue opened with the PR train's merge history attached
- [ ] both ratification questions resolved with the author BEFORE filing — they are internal governance and stay out of the upstream text (political review, finding 2)
- [ ] his response recorded here; fork-vs-upstream decision taken on it

## Amendments (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
Two decisions the RFC text must carry that DESIGN.md underprices: (a) the
memory backend's fate under the per-field FTS schema — per-field BM25 with
column weights is a rewrite of bm25.ts's flat token stream, and "sqlite-only
for v2" is a decision nobody has made out loud; (b) the v2 filename must
mirror multi-tenant suffixing (search-index-<zoteroUserId> today) or N tenants
share one file. Also noted: on the stdio path upstream installs no shutdown
handlers at all (src/index.ts:73-76) — crash-only is the reality, which is an
argument FOR the lease design, stated in the RFC's favor.
